  "name": "Chromatic Overprint — Two-Ink Press",
  "description": "Two independent colour-separated AM spot-ink plates over warm uncoated paper. Revised separation suppresses excess midtone ink, reveals cream stock in highlights, and uses a localized deep-shadow reserve to retain dark subjects without printing dark backgrounds as a uniform violet field. Ink A follows cool colours, Ink B warm colours, and their overlapping dots form the mixed third colour. Each plate has its own rotated 15°/75° halftone grid and source sampling at cell centres. Registration X/Y moves Ink B as a complete plate. Ink Pair: 0 Blue/Orange, 1 Pink/Teal, 2 Indigo/Yellow, 3 Violet/Lime, 4 Black/Fluoro Pink, 5 Navy/Coral. Separation Bias + favours Ink A; - favours Ink B. Dot Scale 5–7 px is useful for photographic detail; 8–12 px produces bolder poster screening. Ink Spread sets dot gain; Paper Grain varies paper and coverage; Effect Mix blends with the source. A single-pass RGB print-style approximation, not physical spot-ink spectral mixing or exportable plates.",
